// Monotonic-read.
//
// A reader sees x's new value and then its old one.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence forbids, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     PC forbids. Coherence forbids it, and PC is stronger.
//     PRAM forbids. MR forbids it, and PRAM is stronger.
//     Causal forbids. CC forbids it, and Causal is stronger.
//     Slow forbids. Local forbids it, and Slow is stronger.
//   the models' definitions:
//     CC forbids. The initial store hb-precedes x = 1, which hb-precedes the
//       second load reading the initial value.
//     Local forbids. The initial value precedes everything in a view, and the
//       view has x = 1 before the first load.
//     POCausal forbids. x = 1 is arbitrated after the initial value, and the
//       second load has seen it.
//     RYW allows. The reader wrote nothing, so read-your-writes asks nothing of
//       it.
//     MR forbids. The second load has seen x = 1 and returns the value it
//       overwrote.
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//     WFR allows. The reader writes nothing, so writes-follow-reads asks
//       nothing of it.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  r0 := x;
  r1 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 0) [RYW, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 0) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, Coherence, RC11,
                           RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, CC, PC, PRAM, Causal, Slow,
                           Local, POCausal, MR]
